      "title": "Sentence 1 — Contrast without exaggeration",
      "text": "**Original:** “It was reporting exceptional growth in the wake of a leadership crisis.” **[P1]**\n\n**Simpler version:** The business was growing very quickly even though it had just experienced a leadership crisis.\n\n**How it works:** *In the wake of* places one development after another and suggests a meaningful connection. The sentence creates tension by placing *exceptional growth* beside *leadership crisis* without claiming the crisis caused the growth.\n\n**Parallel example:** “The city announced a major housing investment in the wake of widespread criticism of its planning policies.”",
