      "title": "Sentence 2 — Separating categories of evidence",
      "text": "**Original:** “This is where readers must draw a distinction between confirmed conduct, reported allegations and evidence of an actual security breach.” **[P3]**\n\n**Simpler version:** At this point, we need to separate established behaviour, unproven claims and proof that security was compromised.\n\n**How it works:** *This is where* introduces the precise point in an argument at which a distinction matters. Three parallel noun phrases create a useful hierarchy of evidence. The phrase *draw a distinction between* is especially valuable in analytical writing.\n\n**Parallel example:** “In debates about screen time, we should draw a distinction between using a device for research, using it for entertainment and using it compulsively.”",
      "paragraph": "P3",
